# shellcheck config for CI's lint-shell job (severity=warning).
#
# These codes are pre-existing, deliberate patterns used consistently across this
# repo's shell scripts, not bugs:
#   SC1007 - `VAR=$(CDPATH= cd -- ... && pwd)` — the space after `CDPATH=` is
#            intentional (clears CDPATH for the subshell only); not an assignment typo.
#   SC2164 - bare `cd`/`pushd`/`popd` inside test-harness subshells (evals/*.test.sh)
#            where the surrounding `set -u` + explicit exit-code assertions already
#            catch a failed directory change.
#   SC2046 - unquoted `$(probe ...)` word-splitting in hooks/guard-worktree.sh is
#            deliberate: probe() prints a fixed two-token "KIND BRANCH" pair to
#            populate positional params via `set --`.
#   SC2088 - the `~/` case arm in hooks/guard-worktree.sh is a literal string match
#            (case pattern), not a tilde expansion the shell is being asked to do.
#   SC2209 - `MODE=command` in hooks/guard-worktree.sh assigns the literal string
#            "command", not the builtin.
#   SC2319 - `$?` immediately after `report "..." $?` in evals/visual-qa.test.sh is
#            read before any intervening command, so it is not stale.
#
# Do not add new codes here to silence a genuinely new warning — fix the script
# instead. Only pre-existing, reviewed patterns belong on this list.
disable=SC1007,SC2164,SC2046,SC2088,SC2209,SC2319
